WEBVTT

00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:03.000
<i>My name is Kakeru Aizawa.</i>

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:04.610
<i>I'm a second year middle schooler.</i>

00:00:04.610 --> 00:00:06.380
<i>Following an accident with a truck,</i>

00:00:07.110 --> 00:00:10.640
<i>my brother, Suguru Aizawa, died.</i>

00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:15.140
<i>Thanks to a heart transplant,</i>

00:00:15.140 --> 00:00:17.370
<i>my life was saved,</i>

00:00:17.370 --> 00:00:18.830
<i>but I quit the soccer club</i>

00:00:18.830 --> 00:00:20.270
<i>and have been spending</i>

00:00:20.270 --> 00:00:22.300
<i>my boring days in rehabilitation.</i>

00:00:23.110 --> 00:00:24.370
<i>Then one day,</i>

00:00:24.370 --> 00:00:28.340
<i>strange things began 
to happen around me...</i>

00:02:01.430 --> 00:02:06.020
<b>Last Pass</b>

00:02:11.560 --> 00:02:12.470
Kakeru?

00:02:13.780 --> 00:02:14.320
What?

00:02:26.930 --> 00:02:29.730
Suguru-san?

00:02:32.780 --> 00:02:34.210
What do you guys think you're doing?

00:02:34.510 --> 00:02:36.560
That's dangerous! Seriously!

00:02:40.370 --> 00:02:42.120
We're terribly sorry.

00:02:43.450 --> 00:02:45.030
Are you injured?

00:02:45.370 --> 00:02:46.850
Is your car all right?

00:02:47.060 --> 00:02:48.130
It's fine.

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:52.560
Just don't play with 
balls around here anymore.

00:02:53.030 --> 00:02:53.780
I understand.

00:02:54.070 --> 00:02:55.510
I'm truly sorry.

00:02:55.820 --> 00:02:57.170
As long as you understand.

00:03:02.700 --> 00:03:03.960
Let's be careful.

00:03:03.960 --> 00:03:04.580
Okay.

00:03:10.480 --> 00:03:14.170
<i>A left kick sent through a tiny 
gap between the children...</i>

00:03:14.860 --> 00:03:17.130
<i>just like Suguru-san.</i>

00:03:18.970 --> 00:03:20.970
Thank you, brother!

00:03:25.280 --> 00:03:27.060
Did I...

00:03:31.520 --> 00:03:32.560
Kakeru...

00:03:44.110 --> 00:03:45.070
<b>Counseling</b>

00:03:47.650 --> 00:03:48.540
How'd it go?

00:03:50.040 --> 00:03:51.000
Doing well.

00:03:52.620 --> 00:03:54.460
Kakeru-kun's heart transplant

00:03:54.960 --> 00:03:56.520
has adapted so well,

00:03:56.520 --> 00:03:57.920
it could be called miraculous.

00:03:59.750 --> 00:04:03.990
However, even colds can cause 
rejection in some cases,

00:04:03.990 --> 00:04:04.810
so be careful.

00:04:04.810 --> 00:04:05.400
Okay.

00:04:05.850 --> 00:04:08.510
Hey, you don't look so well.

00:04:08.810 --> 00:04:10.020
Is anything wrong?

00:04:11.040 --> 00:04:13.060
Have you been sleeping 
all right lately?

00:04:15.410 --> 00:04:16.500
Mishima-san,

00:04:16.860 --> 00:04:17.910
do you have a moment?

00:04:18.270 --> 00:04:19.980
Me?

00:04:21.740 --> 00:04:22.700
I'd like to talk to you.

00:04:23.010 --> 00:04:24.390
O-Okay.

00:04:27.930 --> 00:04:29.330
This is an interesting book.

00:04:31.580 --> 00:04:40.050
<b>The Heart Speaks
Records of recipients of heart transplants</b>

00:04:31.850 --> 00:04:35.210
The recipient of a heart transplant
may start to demonstrate behavior

00:04:35.210 --> 00:04:38.150
that can only be described as
a transplant of the donor's memories.

00:04:38.150 --> 00:04:40.050
It's a collection of those incidents.

00:04:40.520 --> 00:04:41.620
For example,

00:04:41.620 --> 00:04:44.200
starting to like foods that 
one previously disliked,

00:04:44.200 --> 00:04:45.400
or someone unable to swim

00:04:45.400 --> 00:04:46.760
suddenly being able to swim.

00:04:47.370 --> 00:04:50.970
Even seeing the donor's dreams.

00:04:51.270 --> 00:04:53.100
You can't mean to say...

00:04:53.470 --> 00:04:56.140
It hasn't been proven scientifically,

00:04:56.540 --> 00:04:58.410
but there have been a significant

00:04:58.410 --> 00:04:59.940
number of reported cases.

00:05:01.410 --> 00:05:03.360
After observing Kakeru-kun recently,

00:05:03.360 --> 00:05:06.220
have you noticed anything like that?

00:05:07.070 --> 00:05:08.350
I'll ask more directly.

00:05:08.750 --> 00:05:10.090
Have you felt Suguru-san's

00:05:10.090 --> 00:05:12.120
presence inside Kakeru-kun?

00:05:15.430 --> 00:05:17.470
As a childhood friend,

00:05:17.470 --> 00:05:19.230
you should be able to 
notice small changes

00:05:19.230 --> 00:05:21.570
that most people would fail to see.

00:05:22.770 --> 00:05:26.000
Suguru-san's favorite things, 
gestures, and speech patterns:

00:05:26.500 --> 00:05:27.750
have any of these things

00:05:27.750 --> 00:05:30.510
manifested in Kakeru-kun?

00:05:31.100 --> 00:05:34.600
Wh-Why are you talking 
to me about this?

00:05:35.270 --> 00:05:36.240
Because,

00:05:37.550 --> 00:05:40.860
you found out about 
the heart transplant.

00:05:42.970 --> 00:05:45.140
Kakeru is alive because of the heart

00:05:45.140 --> 00:05:47.400
transplanted from his beloved brother.

00:05:48.350 --> 00:05:50.380
<i>Suguru-san's heart...</i>

00:05:51.590 --> 00:05:53.320
<i>was transplanted into Kakeru?!</i>

00:05:58.730 --> 00:05:59.990
I'm sorry.

00:05:59.990 --> 00:06:01.720
I didn't mean to eavesdrop.

00:06:02.020 --> 00:06:03.530
So you did hear, after all.

00:06:03.530 --> 00:06:04.170
What?

00:06:04.600 --> 00:06:06.380
It's fine. Forget about it.

00:06:06.740 --> 00:06:09.130
We were careless, as well.

00:06:10.230 --> 00:06:12.360
I have one request of you.

00:06:13.180 --> 00:06:14.100
What is it?

00:06:14.920 --> 00:06:17.760
If you notice anything 
different about Kakeru-kun,

00:06:17.760 --> 00:06:19.740
I'd like you to let me know.

00:06:20.190 --> 00:06:21.310
It's something that only you,

00:06:21.310 --> 00:06:24.780
<b>The Heart Speaks
Records of recipients of heart transplants</b>

00:06:21.960 --> 00:06:23.890
who's always with him, can do.

00:06:26.520 --> 00:06:28.630
Could you just keep it in mind?

00:06:35.610 --> 00:06:36.700
Is something wrong?

00:06:38.190 --> 00:06:40.670
Oh, no. It's nothing.

00:06:41.220 --> 00:06:42.040
I see.

00:06:45.380 --> 00:06:47.880
<b>Aizawa Family</b>

00:06:48.290 --> 00:06:49.250
<i>Brother...</i>

00:07:02.190 --> 00:07:04.170
Oh, Silver?

00:07:04.490 --> 00:07:06.320
Brazil's U-15 ace,

00:07:06.320 --> 00:07:07.610
Leonardo Silva?

00:07:09.290 --> 00:07:10.610
It's really him!

00:07:10.610 --> 00:07:12.390
But what's he doing here?

00:07:12.390 --> 00:07:14.100
What should I say to him?

00:07:14.100 --> 00:07:14.950
In Portuguese?

00:07:15.360 --> 00:07:16.910
C-Can I have your autograph?

00:07:17.080 --> 00:07:20.020
C'mon, Kakeru! Keep it together.

00:07:20.330 --> 00:07:21.220
Kakeru?

00:07:23.120 --> 00:07:24.660
Suguru's brother?

00:07:24.660 --> 00:07:25.280
What?

00:07:26.180 --> 00:07:27.520
Y-Yes!

00:07:28.310 --> 00:07:29.340
Nice to meet you.

00:07:31.590 --> 00:07:32.760
What? Japanese?

00:07:33.190 --> 00:07:34.300
But why?

00:07:37.940 --> 00:07:40.900
Suguru was my rival and my friend.

00:07:41.770 --> 00:07:42.770
It's a shame.

00:07:43.550 --> 00:07:44.390
Yes...

00:07:54.150 --> 00:07:57.490
By the way, there was 
something Suguru told me.

00:07:57.670 --> 00:07:58.580
What?

00:07:58.580 --> 00:08:02.370
He said the ideal Knight 
in the Area was in Japan.

00:08:04.320 --> 00:08:06.540
He said it was you, Kakeru.

00:08:08.750 --> 00:08:10.050
You're mistaken.

00:08:11.510 --> 00:08:12.930
I believe you're mistaken.

00:08:21.460 --> 00:08:22.290
I see.

00:08:24.150 --> 00:08:25.650
Let's meet again, Kakeru.

00:08:34.080 --> 00:08:35.770
Suguru Aizawa...

00:08:36.230 --> 00:08:38.480
We've lost an amazing player.

00:08:39.180 --> 00:08:40.040
Yeah.

00:08:42.400 --> 00:08:43.040
Leo,

00:08:43.840 --> 00:08:47.030
Japan's soccer holds no 
appeal for you anymore.

00:08:47.030 --> 00:08:48.360
I've said it before,

00:08:48.360 --> 00:08:51.470
but you should join the 
European top club.

00:08:51.920 --> 00:08:53.010
Roberto...

00:08:53.780 --> 00:08:56.930
I met someone interesting 
by Suguru's grave.

00:08:56.930 --> 00:08:57.970
Someone interesting?

00:08:58.600 --> 00:08:59.970
Suguru's knight.

00:09:02.960 --> 00:09:05.960
The knight hasn't awakened yet, huh?

00:09:12.290 --> 00:09:13.240
Hello?

00:09:13.240 --> 00:09:15.380
Hey, it's me. What are you up to?

00:09:15.700 --> 00:09:16.530
Nothing much.

00:09:16.880 --> 00:09:18.530
What about you?

00:09:18.900 --> 00:09:21.380
It's nothing really important, but...

00:09:21.380 --> 00:09:22.750
Spit it out.

00:09:22.750 --> 00:09:25.590
Next Sunday, wanna go 
pick up some girls?

00:09:25.590 --> 00:09:28.000
What? I don't do that stuff.

00:09:28.150 --> 00:09:31.340
C'mon. I'll show you how to do it.

00:09:31.340 --> 00:09:32.620
Leave it to me.

00:09:32.620 --> 00:09:34.950
From hair styling to pick up lines.

00:09:34.950 --> 00:09:37.050
What? I have to style my hair?

00:09:37.450 --> 00:09:38.800
Obviously!

00:09:40.870 --> 00:09:41.530
Kota...

00:09:42.490 --> 00:09:43.620
Thanks.

00:09:44.890 --> 00:09:46.520
Hey, Kakeru.

00:09:47.340 --> 00:09:48.880
Even if you quit the soccer club,

00:09:49.270 --> 00:09:50.940
we're still friends.

00:09:52.250 --> 00:09:53.230
Yeah.

00:09:53.230 --> 00:09:55.240
All right, I'll talk to you later.

00:09:55.240 --> 00:09:57.730
Yeah, I'll see you later.

00:10:14.170 --> 00:10:16.970
<b>Counseling</b>

00:10:15.560 --> 00:10:16.970
You're looking well.

00:10:17.600 --> 00:10:20.060
I was worried about trauma 
from the accident

00:10:20.060 --> 00:10:21.430
or post-op stress.

00:10:21.690 --> 00:10:23.950
Good thing I'm so thickheaded.

00:10:29.520 --> 00:10:32.220
Suguru-san was very delicate

00:10:32.220 --> 00:10:34.860
and he was always about 
to crack under pressure.

00:10:35.320 --> 00:10:36.440
No way...

00:10:36.760 --> 00:10:39.800
He always seemed so 
composed in any situation.

00:10:40.280 --> 00:10:41.740
That's just how he wanted to appear.

00:10:42.680 --> 00:10:44.740
He was just a boy of 15,

00:10:44.740 --> 00:10:48.000
but he was playing with 
the world's eyes on him.

00:10:48.880 --> 00:10:50.360
There's no way something could

00:10:50.360 --> 00:10:51.960
be bothering the great Suguru Aizawa.

00:10:53.610 --> 00:10:55.550
What do you know about me?

00:10:57.470 --> 00:11:00.180
Since a little before the accident,

00:11:00.180 --> 00:11:02.190
he seemed to be having bad dreams.

00:11:02.830 --> 00:11:04.490
Did he tell you about them?

00:11:04.760 --> 00:11:05.560
No.

00:11:05.950 --> 00:11:08.480
Oh, but, about good dreams:

00:11:08.480 --> 00:11:09.770
on the day of accident,

00:11:09.770 --> 00:11:12.180
he told me that he'd had 
the best dream that morning.

00:11:12.180 --> 00:11:12.970
Really?

00:11:13.360 --> 00:11:14.680
Did he tell you what 
kind of dream it was?

00:11:14.680 --> 00:11:15.520
Yes,

00:11:16.480 --> 00:11:17.480
um...

00:11:18.040 --> 00:11:19.900
It was the World Cup finals.

00:11:19.900 --> 00:11:21.450
The score was 0-0 in extra time.

00:11:21.700 --> 00:11:23.870
My brother passed towards 
the front line,

00:11:23.870 --> 00:11:25.740
and the forward who received the pass

00:11:25.740 --> 00:11:26.620
scored a goal.

00:11:27.360 --> 00:11:28.080
And then?

00:11:28.650 --> 00:11:31.250
Then he asked me who I thought

00:11:31.250 --> 00:11:33.340
the forward who received the pass was.

00:11:33.710 --> 00:11:35.000
How did you answer?

00:11:36.070 --> 00:11:37.050
I'm sorry.

00:11:37.870 --> 00:11:40.010
That's when the accident happened.

00:11:42.200 --> 00:11:43.250
I see.

00:11:44.060 --> 00:11:45.390
I'm sorry.

00:11:46.290 --> 00:11:48.470
Have you had any strange dreams?

00:11:49.260 --> 00:11:51.310
No, not in particular.

00:11:51.830 --> 00:11:52.790
That's fine.

00:11:53.280 --> 00:11:55.410
Your heart rate has stabilized, too.

00:11:55.650 --> 00:11:56.400
Is that so?

00:11:57.040 --> 00:11:58.120
Have you put on weight?

00:11:58.120 --> 00:11:58.830
What?

00:11:59.380 --> 00:12:01.830
You have to make sure 
you keep exercising.

00:12:02.290 --> 00:12:04.580
But I don't know what to do...

00:12:04.580 --> 00:12:05.370
Let's see...

00:12:05.670 --> 00:12:07.830
What about soccer?

00:12:08.270 --> 00:12:09.770
That's a little...

00:12:10.280 --> 00:12:12.790
Exercise that you're used to 
is better for rehabilitation.

00:12:13.560 --> 00:12:16.250
You can start with light exercise.

00:12:17.720 --> 00:12:18.730
I see.

00:12:20.040 --> 00:12:21.170
Thanks for the meal.

00:12:21.550 --> 00:12:23.130
Are you done already?

00:12:23.520 --> 00:12:25.090
Did it taste bad?

00:12:25.090 --> 00:12:26.270
No.

00:12:59.160 --> 00:13:00.870
It's for rehabilitation.

00:13:29.950 --> 00:13:31.300
Give me a break!

00:13:31.580 --> 00:13:33.150
Who are you?

00:13:33.150 --> 00:13:34.330
What do you want?

00:13:42.440 --> 00:13:43.260
Not again!

00:13:48.820 --> 00:13:49.640
This guy...

00:13:51.420 --> 00:13:52.600
He's making fun of me!

00:14:01.630 --> 00:14:02.360
Left?

00:14:09.570 --> 00:14:10.750
Show me...

00:14:14.130 --> 00:14:15.260
who you really are!

00:14:18.560 --> 00:14:19.640
<i>A girl?!</i>

00:14:24.530 --> 00:14:26.510
S-Sorry, I got carried away.

00:14:32.110 --> 00:14:32.990
What?

00:14:34.520 --> 00:14:35.560
No way!

00:14:36.350 --> 00:14:37.780
Seven?!

00:14:58.780 --> 00:15:00.370
I'm sorry, Kakeru.

00:15:01.030 --> 00:15:02.210
Why?

00:15:02.210 --> 00:15:03.860
More importantly, did you notice?

00:15:04.990 --> 00:15:07.680
Just now, you shot with your left.

00:15:10.890 --> 00:15:13.020
It was an amazing volley shot,

00:15:13.020 --> 00:15:13.800
just like...

00:15:15.210 --> 00:15:17.800
<i>Yeah, it was just like...</i>

00:15:21.240 --> 00:15:23.110
It was a favor for your brother.

00:15:23.810 --> 00:15:24.900
My brother?

00:15:25.380 --> 00:15:29.890
The U-15 team went to 
Mexico once, right?

00:15:30.440 --> 00:15:32.640
I went too, to cheer them on.

00:15:33.170 --> 00:15:34.070
Suguru-san!

00:15:37.620 --> 00:15:38.700
I see.

00:15:38.700 --> 00:15:40.540
It must be nostalgic to return to Japan.

00:15:40.800 --> 00:15:44.250
I'm planning on transferring 
to your school in the winter.

00:15:44.250 --> 00:15:46.740
Hey, is Kakeru doing his best?

00:15:46.740 --> 00:15:49.530
Will he be on the youth
 representative team by next year?

00:15:49.530 --> 00:15:52.330
He's the manager right now.

00:15:52.330 --> 00:15:53.000
What?

00:15:53.440 --> 00:15:55.650
Just because he wasn't a 
regular his first year.

00:15:55.950 --> 00:15:57.480
I don't know what he's thinking.

00:15:59.560 --> 00:16:03.350
I wonder if having an 
amazing brother like you

00:16:03.350 --> 00:16:05.010
is just too much pressure.

00:16:05.010 --> 00:16:06.210
Hey, Seven.

00:16:07.330 --> 00:16:11.490
If you come to our school, 
I have a favor to ask of you.

00:16:12.170 --> 00:16:14.560
Suguru-san apparently knew that

00:16:14.560 --> 00:16:17.080
you secretly practiced in the park.

00:16:17.860 --> 00:16:20.760
So he asked me to be 
your practice partner.

00:16:25.040 --> 00:16:26.240
Hey, Kakeru...

00:16:27.660 --> 00:16:29.340
There was something

00:16:29.340 --> 00:16:31.380
that I was going to tell you,
 if you came today.

00:16:32.360 --> 00:16:36.760
After that accident, 
you were saved by a heart transplant.

00:16:37.480 --> 00:16:39.310
That heart belonged to...

00:16:43.910 --> 00:16:45.000
Suguru-san.

00:16:52.530 --> 00:16:54.280
Suguru-san...

00:16:55.090 --> 00:16:57.020
Suguru-san gave you your life.

00:16:58.130 --> 00:17:01.330
S-So I...

00:17:01.770 --> 00:17:06.300
So I stole my brother's life.

00:17:06.300 --> 00:17:07.000
No!

00:17:07.500 --> 00:17:09.540
Suguru-san was brain dead

00:17:09.540 --> 00:17:11.960
and would have died anyway.

00:17:12.490 --> 00:17:13.830
Neither one of you

00:17:13.830 --> 00:17:16.210
would have made it without this.

00:17:20.310 --> 00:17:21.270
Right here...

00:17:21.940 --> 00:17:23.450
Right here, Kakeru.

00:17:24.120 --> 00:17:28.610
Along with his heart, lies 
Suguru-san's unfulfilled dreams.

00:17:29.070 --> 00:17:32.230
Suguru-san left you his dreams.

00:17:36.310 --> 00:17:38.670
Kakeru. Hey, Kakeru.

00:17:38.670 --> 00:17:40.940
Don't say you'll quit soccer.

00:17:41.240 --> 00:17:43.160
You can't quit soccer.

00:17:51.090 --> 00:17:52.250
Kakeru!

00:18:06.420 --> 00:18:07.350
Kakeru?

00:18:07.870 --> 00:18:09.610
Kakeru, what happened?

00:18:09.610 --> 00:18:10.810
Kakeru!

00:18:49.960 --> 00:18:51.170
Brother...

00:18:56.130 --> 00:18:57.270
His diary?

00:19:05.800 --> 00:19:09.360
<i>Regarding the problem of 
hardening the defense,</i>

00:19:09.360 --> 00:19:11.530
<i>we're finally seeing the results 
of the special training.</i>

00:19:12.000 --> 00:19:13.780
<i>It isn't quite Catenaccio,</i>

00:19:13.780 --> 00:19:15.250
<i>but it doesn't feel bad.</i>

00:19:16.040 --> 00:19:18.740
<i>Today, I saw the video 
of the Brazil match.</i>

00:19:19.290 --> 00:19:20.970
<i>If Japan is satisfied with a tie,</i>

00:19:20.970 --> 00:19:24.430
<i>then I doubt they'll ever 
bring home the World Cup.</i>

00:19:25.830 --> 00:19:28.540
Unsurprisingly, there's 
nothing but soccer...

00:19:30.150 --> 00:19:31.910
<i>Both the national team and the U-15 team</i>

00:19:31.910 --> 00:19:33.480
<i>are missing the same thing.</i>

00:19:33.740 --> 00:19:35.150
<i>We need a player who can</i>

00:19:35.150 --> 00:19:37.440
<i>do his job properly in the penalty area.</i>

00:19:37.440 --> 00:19:39.900
A knight in the area.

00:19:38.110 --> 00:19:39.440
<i>A knight in the area.</i>

00:19:43.870 --> 00:19:46.470
<i>I had that dream again this morning.</i>

00:19:47.000 --> 00:19:50.110
<i>During a match, I realize 
there's no one else around.</i>

00:19:50.400 --> 00:19:51.570
<i>I'm all alone.</i>

00:19:52.050 --> 00:19:54.840
<i>I call and I call, but no one responds.</i>

00:19:56.030 --> 00:19:57.590
<i>I wake up in a sweat.</i>

00:19:58.020 --> 00:19:59.790
<i>I'm afraid to sleep.</i>

00:20:05.360 --> 00:20:06.680
It's the day of the accident.

00:20:07.360 --> 00:20:09.490
<i>For the first time in ages,
 I woke up from a good dream.</i>

00:20:10.020 --> 00:20:11.850
<i>I'm in a great mood.</i>

00:20:12.300 --> 00:20:13.840
<i>It's the World Cup finals.</i>

00:20:14.260 --> 00:20:15.920
<i>The score is 0-0 in extra time.</i>

00:20:39.010 --> 00:20:40.010
<i>Kakeru!</i>

00:20:45.260 --> 00:20:46.910
<i>That becomes the winning point</i>

00:20:47.270 --> 00:20:50.850
<i>and Kakeru and I raise the trophy.</i>

00:20:51.630 --> 00:20:53.980
<i>The dream that I've always had.</i>

00:20:54.450 --> 00:20:56.140
<i>Kakeru's and my dream!</i>

00:20:57.140 --> 00:20:58.290
Brother...

00:20:59.050 --> 00:21:00.080
Brother...

00:21:01.070 --> 00:21:02.200
Brother...

00:21:05.510 --> 00:21:06.650
Brother...

00:21:08.890 --> 00:21:10.150
I'm sorry to bother you

00:21:10.150 --> 00:21:11.740
on the morning of your day off.

00:21:11.740 --> 00:21:12.770
It's fine,

00:21:12.770 --> 00:21:16.470
but Kakeru left early this morning.

00:21:16.470 --> 00:21:18.170
What? Where to?

00:21:18.170 --> 00:21:20.210
He just suddenly left 
without telling me where.

00:21:21.360 --> 00:21:22.610
Is there something wrong?

00:21:23.040 --> 00:21:23.920
No.

00:21:24.530 --> 00:21:25.480
Excuse me.

00:21:25.480 --> 00:21:26.180
Nana-chan?

00:21:44.300 --> 00:21:45.450
Kakeru...

00:21:53.310 --> 00:21:56.030
Brother, I remembered.

00:21:56.030 --> 00:21:57.450
It was yours and mine.

00:21:57.450 --> 00:21:58.540
Our dream.

00:22:02.130 --> 00:22:03.270
<i>Kakeru?</i>

00:22:07.390 --> 00:22:09.440
I won't run away anymore!

00:22:12.750 --> 00:22:15.160
I'll keep playing soccer

00:22:15.160 --> 00:22:18.040
as long as this life I received 
from my brother goes on.

00:22:20.070 --> 00:22:21.940
Really, Kakeru?

00:22:23.580 --> 00:22:24.620
Seven!

00:22:25.150 --> 00:22:26.280
What are you doing here?

00:22:33.790 --> 00:22:34.930
I received it.

00:22:36.180 --> 00:22:38.110
My brother's last pass.

00:22:39.440 --> 00:22:40.860
Right here.

00:22:42.290 --> 00:22:43.420
I'm so glad...

00:22:43.900 --> 00:22:45.000
Kakeru...

00:22:46.570 --> 00:22:47.940
I...

00:23:02.790 --> 00:23:04.620
Isn't this Suguru-san's diary?

00:23:04.620 --> 00:23:05.730
Look here. Here.

00:23:06.150 --> 00:23:09.060
<i>It will be nostalgic to 
meet with Ryuichi Araki.</i>

00:23:09.420 --> 00:23:12.430
<i>This time I want him to join 
the representative team.</i>

00:23:12.820 --> 00:23:15.200
<i>Araki's passing intuition 
is better than mine...</i>

00:23:15.820 --> 00:23:16.710
No way.

00:23:17.110 --> 00:23:20.670
A midfielder the same age as
Suguru-san, with a better pass?

00:23:22.070 --> 00:23:25.680
<i>The day I first met Araki 
at the U-15 training camp,</i>

00:23:25.680 --> 00:23:27.290
<i>I remember clearly, even today.</i>

00:23:32.930 --> 00:23:34.510
He's an interesting guy, right?

00:23:35.060 --> 00:23:36.020
Coach?

00:23:36.020 --> 00:23:39.200
Ryuichi Araki. 
He's the same age as you.

00:23:39.830 --> 00:23:41.350
Hey, Araki!

00:23:46.550 --> 00:23:48.510
<i>I felt that an amazing 
guy had come along.</i>

00:23:48.510 --> 00:23:50.070
<i>His unique pass...</i>

00:23:50.630 --> 00:23:52.150
<i>An unexpected positioning</i>

00:23:52.150 --> 00:23:53.530
<i>and an intuition that creates chances.</i>

00:23:56.510 --> 00:23:59.950
<i>He's the kind of guy 
they call a fantasista.</i>

00:23:59.950 --> 00:24:01.670
<i>I was surprised by his swiftness.</i>

00:24:02.210 --> 00:24:06.670
Araki decided to go to 
Enoshima High School.

00:24:02.610 --> 00:24:04.290
He goes to high school...

00:24:07.210 --> 00:24:10.020
I'm going to play soccer 
at that high school.

00:24:10.460 --> 00:24:11.920
I want to try to receive Araki's pass,

00:24:11.920 --> 00:24:13.890
that my brother admired.

00:24:14.290 --> 00:24:17.350
A knight in the area needs a king!

00:24:21.270 --> 00:24:22.310
Kakeru,

00:24:22.830 --> 00:24:25.270
I want to go to the 
same high school as you.

00:24:26.850 --> 00:24:27.980
I can, right?

00:24:29.890 --> 00:24:30.910
Yeah.

00:24:31.560 --> 00:24:32.600
Of course!

00:24:45.940 --> 00:25:15.400
<b>Next time: Enoshima High Football Club?!</b>

00:24:47.550 --> 00:24:50.100
Kakeru Aizawa, overcoming 
the death of his brother,

00:24:50.100 --> 00:24:52.560
successfully enrolls in 
Enoshima High School,

00:24:52.560 --> 00:24:55.560
where the genius passer, 
Ryuichi Araki, attends.

00:24:54.530 --> 00:24:56.010
<b>Enoshima High FC</b>

00:24:56.010 --> 00:24:57.810
Kakeru immediately 
joins the soccer club

00:24:57.810 --> 00:25:00.020
and is subjected to a 
strange initiation.

00:25:00.390 --> 00:25:02.440
Full of expectation and hope,

00:25:02.440 --> 00:25:04.440
Kakeru learns a startling truth

00:25:04.440 --> 00:25:05.980
from a kind upperclassman.

00:25:06.420 --> 00:25:07.980
Next time on 
The Knight in the Area:

00:25:07.980 --> 00:25:11.490
the fourth episode,
 "Enoshima High Football Club?!"

00:25:12.140 --> 00:25:14.750
Hey, Kakeru, who's this guy?
